    <name>
      <text>Partial Variation 4 - Taxi fare graph (interactive)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A taxi in Nairobi charges a fixed booking fee plus a charge for every kilometre travelled: \(C = kd + b\), where \(C\) is the cost in hundreds of Ksh and \(d\) is the distance in km. The graph shows this relationship, and \(P\) is a point on the line.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans3="ans3Ref" width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
board.create('text', [7.6, 1.5, 'd (km)'], {fixed:true});
board.create('text', [0.2, 36.5, 'C (Ksh 100s)'], {fixed:true});
var line = board.create('segment', [[0,{#pb#}],[9,{#pb+9*pk#}]], {strokeColor:'blue', fixed:true});
var P = board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pCP#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4});
var A = board.create('point', [1,1], {name:'A', snapToGrid:true, snapSizeX:1, snapSizeY:1, size:5});
stack_jxg.bind_point(ans3Ref, A);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p>(a) Read from the graph where the line crosses the vertical axis. This is the fixed booking fee, \(b\), in hundreds of Ksh.</p>
<p>\(b = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Use the point \(P\) and your value of \(b\) to find the rate \(k\), the cost for each km in hundreds of Ksh.</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>(c) Drag the point \(A\) to the point on the line where \(d = {@px3@}\) km. The coordinates of \(A\) appear in the box below.</p>
<p>\(A = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p><strong>(a) Find the booking fee \(b\)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: read where the line crosses the vertical axis.</strong> On the vertical axis \(d = 0\), and substituting \(d = 0\) into \(C = kd + b\) gives \(C = b\). So the value where the line crosses the vertical axis is \(b\). The graph crosses at \(C = {@pb@}\), so</p>
\[ b = {@pb@}. \]
<p>The cost is in hundreds of Ksh, so the booking fee is Ksh \({@100*pb@}\). It is what you pay before travelling any distance.</p>

<p><strong>(b) Find the rate \(k\)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: read the coordinates of \(P\) from the graph.</strong> \(P\) is at \(d = {@pr@}\) km and \(C = {@pCP@}\), so \(P = ({@pr@}, {@pCP@})\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: substitute \(P\) and \(b = {@pb@}\) into \(C = kd + b\).</strong></p>
\[ {@pCP@} = {@pr@}k + {@pb@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 3: subtract \({@pb@}\) from both sides.</strong></p>
\[ {@pCP@} - {@pb@} = {@pr@}k \quad\Longrightarrow\quad {@pCP-pb@} = {@pr@}k. \]
<p><strong>Step 4: divide both sides by \({@pr@}\).</strong></p>
\[ k = \frac{ {@pCP-pb@} }{ {@pr@} } = {@pk@}. \]
<p>So each kilometre costs \({@pk@}\) hundred Ksh, that is Ksh \({@100*pk@}\).</p>

<p><strong>(c) Find the point \(A\) on the line where \(d = {@px3@}\)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: write the equation of the line using \(k\) and \(b\).</strong></p>
\[ C = {@pk@}d + {@pb@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 2: substitute \(d = {@px3@}\).</strong></p>
\[ C = {@pk@} \times {@px3@} + {@pb@} = {@pk*px3@} + {@pb@} = {@pk*px3+pb@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 3: write down the coordinates of \(A\).</strong> On the graph, go along the horizontal axis to \(d = {@px3@}\), then straight up to the line. The line is at \(C = {@pk*px3+pb@}\), so</p>
\[ A = ({@px3@}, {@pk*px3+pb@}). \]<h3>Worked Solution</h3>


[[jsxgraph width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
board.create('segment', [[0,{#pb#}],[9,{#pb+9*pk#}]], {strokeColor:'blue', fixed:true});
board.create('point', [0,{#pb#}], {name:'b', fixed:true, color:'#444', size:3, label:{offset:[10,-10], anchorX:'left'}});
board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pCP#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4, label:{offset:[-10,10], anchorX:'right'}});
board.create('point', [{#px3#},{#pk*px3+pb#}], {name:'A', fixed:true, color:'green', size:4, label:{offset:[10,-10], anchorX:'left'}});
board.create('segment', [[{#px3#},0],[{#px3#},{#pk*px3+pb#}]], {dash:2, strokeColor:'#888', fixed:true});
board.create('segment', [[0,{#pk*px3+pb#}],[{#px3#},{#pk*px3+pb#}]], {dash:2, strokeColor:'#888', fixed:true});
[[/jsxgraph]]]]></text>
